\nThe negation of $A$ can be written as\n\n- $¬A:$ You buy a ticket.\n\nTherefore, the given statement is logically equivalent to the following:\n\n$\\,$ You buy a ticket, or you cannot enter the concert.\n\nWe can write this in more everyday language as follows:\n\n$\\,$ Buy a ticket, or you cannot enter the concert." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401730 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401731 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401730 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401732 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401730 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401733 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401730 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401734 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401730 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401735 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401730 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401730 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401730 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186401731 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401730 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8f6ea998-1510-5ac2-a229-6d71f403c27f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401731 #edb/ref 1080 "Buy a ticket, or you cannot enter the concert." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401731 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401731 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "34a0563d-13f2-5256-b18a-47d8b5f64041" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401732 #edb/ref 1080 "Buy a ticket, and you cannot enter the concert." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401732 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401732 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f6731b6b-f0cf-55d7-87cc-7c66343c06ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401733 #edb/ref 1080 "Don't buy a ticket, or you can enter the concert." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401733 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401733 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d0b9de9c-dfe1-5e38-920b-ffe3d2c1e6b3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401734 #edb/ref 1080 "Don't buy a ticket, and you cannot enter the conce